{
  "dom_id": "step-q110969",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 0=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=12.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$",
